      "text": [
        " : سُئِلَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلسَّائِبَةِ قَالَ \"هُوَ اَلرَّجُلُ يُعْتِقُ غُلاَمَهُ ثُمَّ يَقُولُ لَهُ اِذْهَبْ حَيْثُ شِئْتَ لَيْسَ لِي مِنْ مِيرَاثِكَ شَيْءٌ وَ لاَ عَلَيَّ مِنْ جَرِيرَتِكَ شَيْءٌ وَ يُشْهِدُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ شَاهِدَيْنِ \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3502 - Al-Hasan ibn Mahbub narrated from Khalid ibn Jarir, from Abu al-Rabi', who said:\nAbu Abdullah (as), was asked about al-sa'ibah (a freed slave who is left without ties).\nImam (as) said: \"He is a man who frees his slave and then says to him, 'Go wherever you wish. I have no share in your inheritance, nor am I responsible for any liability on your behalf.' He must have two witnesses testify to this declaration.\""
        ]
      }
